## SECTION 9: STOPPING RULES FOR OPTIMIZATION

Stop the next training run when any of these conditions are met:

| Condition | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Fitness improves by < 0.001 for 10 consecutive generations | **STOP** – Hit local plateau |
| Brier score starts increasing (after decreasing) | **STOP** – Overfitting detected |
| Any parameter exceeds hard bounds (e.g., w_mfg_pen < -1.0) | **RESTART** – Bounds violated |
| Same confusion matrix (tp/fn) appears in top 5 models for 5 generations | **PAUSE** – Check for mode collapse |
| Runtime > 12 hours | **STOP** – Diminishing returns |

